<spell-notebook "panel theming">
	<header level="1">
		Panel
		<header>A panel is an inspector:  a tinted box of fields under a header band, with sub-head bands that open and close.</>
	</>
	<panel-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a `--ui-panel-*` token on the panel, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow root.
			The colour defaults come from the panel's hue (`color`, else `primary`). The section's own tokens
			(`--ui-section-tip-*`, the chevron's turn) apply too. Never set the `--_ui-panel-*` names: they're
			the sheet's private plumbing. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-panel" playground>
				<ui-panel label="Color Set" collapsible style="max-width: 320px">
					<ui-input placeholder="Name, e.g. brand" aria-label="Set name"></>
					<ui-panel label="Tweak" collapsible>
						<ui-slider min="0" max="200" step="20" value="100" aria-label="Vibrancy"></>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Panel is ours, not Fomantic's:  it follows the theme's hues, surfaces and colour scheme.  The Spell
			theme (`spell`) adds the `accent` hue, the brand's soft shadow and the aubergine info tip.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
